-- The days of uses a new database starts with (T143): 0.15's uses go in a partition of their day (0022), made ahead by the checkpointer once it runs (`daysAround`, packages/vault/src/log-checkpointer.ts), and until it has, a use at a time no day holds fails ("no partition of relation log_uses found for row"). A deployment's pipeline migrates before it deploys, so this is the first thing there is: yesterday's (the fence's floor starts three seconds before the migration, which may be just before midnight), today's and the next three, the same days `daysAround` makes. A checkpointer down for longer than the end of today + 3 leaves the days it stopped at (its alarm says so). It only adds partitions, which the previous release's code never touches; and runs once, as the one migration that has it, so later releases' days are the checkpointer's.
SELECT make_day(d::date) FROM generate_series((now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC')::date - 1, (now() AT TIME ZONE 'UTC')::date + 3, interval '1 day') AS d;
